            title: 'Tiddly-Wink American',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Tiddly-Wink American is a domino connecting game from the Block game family. Each player is dealt three tiles from a double-six set; play forms a single arm. Playing a double grants an optional second play. The player who dominoes wins the pool, or the lowest pip count wins if blocked.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Country/Region of Origin: USA\nTime Period: Early 1900s\nHistorical Development: The game evolved from traditional card games in the region\nCultural Significance: Popular social and family game',
              },
            ],
          },
